raygui
------
  Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raygui
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license (the same license as this project).

  This project DOES vendor and redistribute raygui. vendor/raygui.h is an
  unmodified copy of upstream's single-file header at revision
  5.0-9-gfbf5d95, and vendor/styles/*.rgs are unmodified copies of six of
  upstream's style themes.

  raygui is a header-only library, so there is no shared library to install
  and no package-manager formula for it. vendor/raygui_impl.c is the one
  compilation unit that instantiates the implementation; `bb lib:build`
  compiles it into lib/libraygui.dylib. Vendoring the header is what pins
  the version and makes that build reproducible.

  Four examples in src/net/b12n/raygui_jlt/ are Clojure ports of raygui's own
  example programs: scroll-panel, floating-window, custom-input-box and
  style-selector. Those are likewise zlib/libpng licensed, and this project
  is released under the same license so that the original terms carry
  through.

raylib
------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  This project does not vendor or redistribute raylib itself: it loads the
  system-installed libraylib shared library at runtime over its C ABI, and
  links lib/libraygui.dylib against that same library.

  src/net/b12n/raygui_jlt/raylib.clj is a trimmed derivative of the raylib
  bindings in the sibling project b12n-raylib-jlt, carrying only the window,
  frame, input, colour and text surface these examples need.
